A Voidheart is an orb about two feet across, lit from within with a violet glow and cased in overlapping dark scales that keep shifting under the hand. It hangs where it is set, held by a heavy inertia that resists being moved, and it carries on once it is. Standing near one feels like standing in the fane of a [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart]].

Each one sits on the far side of a tear in the [[Phenomena/Weave|weave]], past a room that mirrors a room of the real world, above a great hand that has pulled itself out of the ground while the void-things around it crawl toward it. A hard thing to lift, a Voidheart is worth a great deal of power to a Heart that can take it in.

The Party has taken two. The first they brought out through the tear that opened over the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]]'s dance floor; half of it was broken down and fed to the Heart [[Org/Iconoclasm/Eerie|Eerie]], which kept a seed of its magic-dampening nature. The second they pulled from a portal in the ruined town at the strider's prow, and [[Org/Iconoclasm/Eerie|Eerie]] took all of it as void rather than as fuel.
